@robbensinger @MasterTimBlais Bayesianity is about how you form your own opinions.

Treating truth as sacred is (mostly) about how you speak and act.

And also about actively pursuing the truth (which bayesianity actively discourages, as Yudkowsky points out).

@ESRogs @yashkaf If someone tells you "my biggest flaw is that I forget how much smarter I am than everyone else", and then makes false claims about how smart they are, you'd think less of them.

If a community does so, you'd think less of that community.

Expressing dissent helps mitigate that.

@ESYudkowsky I was actually hoping for links to studies or reports, but I should have expected that people would mainly want to share personal stories.

